posts.body:
I'd like to bring this one back up after a bit.
After putting my project aside for a couple weeks, I've come back to it, realizing that the MOG Event Indicators plugin I was using didn't in fact work as I'd hoped. Because they're registered when the events are registered on scene start (so far as I know), the indicators don't actually appear if new events are spawned with indicators--this means I couldn't readily make the text appear wherever I wanted. I tried a few workarounds with no luck.
However, I've found another similar plugin.
Chaucer's Simple Popups
does exactly what I want--text above event, custom colors, custom size, floats upwards, and fades out--and it was a fairly simple modification to give messages starting opacity (even if the rest of it is pretty complex).
But unfortunately it also layers below the shadows because it exists on the Character Sprites layer, and I'm not exactly sure how to change its container position because it starts from Sprite_Character instead of a larger container.
As seen on line 528, the popup container is created and then addChild-'d to Sprite_Character.
JavaScript:
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$.alias.S_C_p_initialize = Sprite_Character.prototype.initialize;
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Sprite_Character.prototype.initialize = function ( character )
  { // Alias of initialize
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    $.alias.S_C_p_initialize.call( this, character  );
    this._popupSprites = [];
    this._popupContainer = new Sprite();
    this.addChild( this._popupContainer );
  };
My hope is that it'll just be a simple change, but I'm prepared if it's something like somehow replacing all of the Sprite_Character references and trying to work around whatever errors are caused.
I'm also wondering if there isn't another way to go about re-layering. Maybe to co-opt the Sprite_Popups and independently attach them to events through some new function and then create a script call to make them show up.
I've been working at this for a couple weekends, but I think it's clear I need the help.
